  "term": "transsynaptic degeneration",
  "definition": "Transsynaptic degeneration is secondary neurodegeneration that develops in regions remote from a primary site of damage and spreads across synaptic connections between anatomically connected neurons, and sometimes between neurons that are not directly connected, in pathological conditions.",
